</div></section>
<section class="block"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><h2 class="section-title">Careful public-positioning note.</h2><p>This page describes Information-Stationary Locking as a control architecture concept with natural applicability to atom interferometry. It is not a claim that ISL has already been validated in cold-atom hardware. The signal is phase, the useful information is statistical, and environmental disturbance can dominate real instruments. Validation for atom-interferometric embodiments still has to come from a lab — ideally in partnership with a group that operates the relevant hardware.</p></div></div></section>
